#
# The kernel the entry image boots: Apple's RELEASE kernel plus the one filesystem that can be root
# on a device with no storage driver.
#
# Experiment 459 needs two things of this configuration and nothing else, and both are *words* in
# a configuration file rather than code:
#
#   mockfs    - `bsd/miscfs/mockfs/` is the only filesystem in the tree whose `vfc_mountroot` is
#               non-NULL (`bsd/vfs/vfs_conf.c`'s `vfstbllist`; devfs and routefs have neither a
#               mountroot nor VFC_VFSCANMOUNTROOT, and NFSCLIENT is off in this configuration).
#               `vfs_mountroot` therefore skips every other entry and mounts mockfs over whatever
#               `rootdev` names - which is how a kernel with no HFS, no BlockStorage and no eMMC
#               driver gets a root filesystem at all. Apple's own comment for the option in
#               `config/MASTER:123` says what it is for: "Boot from an executable".
#
# This is `RELEASE` by *composition*, not by copy: a configuration's attributes may themselves be
# configuration names (tools/xnu_config/expand.sh), so `[ RELEASE mockfs ]` reuses MASTER.arm's own
# RELEASE attribute list rather than restating it, and one option is added to it. A second copy of
# that list here would be the "one value, two definitions" defect this project has recorded
# twenty times.
#
#  STAGE90_XNU = [ RELEASE mockfs ]
